# Visible work rule: browser open + screenshot proof (MANDATORY, always-on)

The user cannot see what you are doing unless you show it. This rule is **not optional** and has **no "quick change" exception**.

## How to open the page (this laptop)

Use **Cursor's internal / Simple Browser on this machine** — not an external Chrome window as the only proof, and **not** "Browser MCP unavailable → stop".

1. **Preferred:** `cursor-app-control` → `open_resource` with the live (or local) `https://…` / `http://…` URL so the page opens in Cursor next to the agent.
2. If `cursor-ide-browser` MCP tools (`browser_navigate`, `browser_take_screenshot`, etc.) are listed and ready, use those too for navigate + screenshot.
3. If those MCP tools are **not** in the catalog, **do not stop and do not write that MCP is unavailable**. Keep the tab open via `open_resource`, then capture proof on **this Windows laptop** with Playwright / Edge / Chrome headless (e.g. `npx playwright screenshot …`) and save under `.cursor/local/` or a temp path.
4. Tell the user in one line which page you opened so they can watch it.

Default target: **https://app.sync2dine.io** (live). Local only when the user asks: `http://localhost:5174/...`.

## After every change

5. After **each** UI change lands (hot reload or deploy): refresh / re-open that same URL, then take a **new screenshot**.
6. **Embed the screenshot inline** in your reply (`![what changed](path)`). The user relies on these print-screens.
7. **Never** write "done", "fixed", "updated", or similar for a UI change without an accompanying screenshot of the page.

## Forbidden excuses

- Do **not** say "Browser MCP isn't available in this session" and skip proof.
- Do **not** claim the laptop cannot take screenshots — it can (`open_resource` + Playwright/Edge on this PC).

## Page defaults

| Task | Open in Cursor browser |
|------|------------------------|
| Any component/page/style edit | the exact route that renders it |
| Phone / outbound / Call Centre | `https://app.sync2dine.io/calls` |
| Marketing / landing pages | the specific landing path on live |
| AI Studio / Cynthia | the matching `/ai-studio` route |
| Platform / CRM / ops | the matching `/platform/...` or `/crm` path |
| After SPA deploy | re-open the same URL, screenshot again |
